 the  old stuff the only Watergate irid detail  you really need to know  to appreciate this column is the 1969  drunk driving incident in which Senator  Ted Kennedy's passenger Mary Jo Kopechne  II was killed at Chappaquiddick Island  in Massachusetts some have tried to  update the Buckwald column to put in  trumpian references it doesn't quite  work that we will offer a few updates by  the use of illustrations so in homage  and gratitude to buckwalds great  political insight to say nothing of his  remarkable post mortem political  foresight  I will now read this column which  appeared under a variety of titles most  of which were variations on the one in  Los Angeles oh yeah what about  Chappaquiddick these are difficult times  for people who are defending the Nixon  administration no matter where they go  they are attacked by pseudo liberals  McGovern lovers heterosexual  constitutionalists and paranoid John  Dean believers as a public service I am  printing instant responses for loyal  Nicks and nights when they are attacked  at a party please cut it out and carry  it in your pocket one  everyone does it - what about  Chappaquiddick three a president can't  keep track of everything his staff does  for the press is blowing the whole thing  up five whatever Nixon did was for  national security six the Democrats are  sore because they lost the election  seven are you gonna believe a rat like  John Dean or the President of the United  States eight wait til all the facts come  out nine what about Chappaquiddick 10 if  you impeach Nixon you get Agnew 11 the  only thing wrong with Watergate is they  got caught 12 what about Daniel Ellsberg  stealing the Pentagon Papers 13 it  happens in Europe all the time 14 people  would be against Nixon no matter what he  did  15 I'd rather have a crook in the White  House than a fool 16 LBJ used to read  FBI reports every  right 17 what's the big deal about  finding out what your opposition is up  to 18 the president was too busy running  the country to know what was going on 19  what about Chappaquiddick 20 people who  live in glass houses shouldn't throw  stones 21 McGovern would have lost  anyway 22 maybe the committee for the  re-election of the president went a  little too far but they were just a  bunch of eager kids 23 I'm not for  breaking any law but sometimes you have  to do it to save the country 24 Nixon  made a mistake he's only human  25 do you realize what Watergate is  doing to the dollar abroad 26 what about  Harry Truman in the Deep Freeze scandal  27 Franklin D Roosevelt did a lot of  worse things 28 I'm sick and tired of  hearing about Watergate and so is  everybody else  29 this thing should be tried in the  courts and not on television 30 when  Nixon gives his explanation of what  happened there are gonna be a lot of  people in this country with Ag on their  faces 31 my country right or wrong 32  what about Chappaquiddick 33 I think the  people who make all this fuss about  Watergate should be shot 34 if the  Democrats had the money they would have  done the same thing  35 I never trusted Haldeman and  Ehrlichman to start with 36 if you say  one more word about Watergate I'll punch  you in the nose 36 a if the person is  bigger than you if you say one more word  about Watergate I'm leaving this house  36 B if it's your own house and the  person is bigger than you what about  Chappaquiddick by part Buckwald it is  safe to say that in 1973 Donald Trump  did not read this column in ruminating  on buckwalds number 17 what's the big  deal about finding out what your  position is up - it is safe to say that  nobody in the Trump campaign ever read  this column and it is safe to guess that  word Trump himself confronted with  buckwalds masterpiece today his  likeliest response would be that art  buchwald is an example of somebody who's  done an amazing job and is getting  recognized more and more I noticed and  why isn't he writing about crooked  Hillary resists remove piece

